[Heading1]	Simple Benefits
[Normal]	Reconstructed from Oracle's documentation of the SimpleBenefits example rulebase (see README.md).
[Heading2]	Low income allowance
[OPM-conclusion]	the claimant is eligible for the low income allowance if
[OPM-level1]	the claimant is a public housing client and
[OPM-level1]	the claimant's annual income < 20000
[Normal]	The amount is reconstructed: Oracle publishes 70 for a claimant with two children, not the rule.
[OPM-conclusion]	the claimant's low income allowance amount = 50 + (10 * InstanceCount(the claimant's children)) if
[OPM-level1]	the claimant is eligible for the low income allowance
[Heading2]	Teenage child allowance
[OPM-conclusion]	the claimant is eligible for the teenage child allowance if
[OPM-level1]	Exists(the claimant's children, the child is a teenager)
[OPM-conclusion]	the child is a teenager if
[OPM-level1]	the child's age >= 13 and
[OPM-level1]	the child's age <= 19
